    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1108">

                <pb facs="1006" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/855</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grevstad</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-28">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 28, 1914</hi>.</date>[<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Received November 28</hi>.] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 761]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to despatch No. 757 of October
                    26, 1914, relating to secret installations for wireless telegraphy recently
                    discovered in the River Plate, I have the honor to forward in duplicate copy,
                    with translation, of an Executive decree of October 20 by which it is forbidden
                    to establish without permission granted by the Executive private radiographic
                    installations in Uruguay either on land or on Uruguayan vessels; which forbids
                    vessels to use their apparatus for wireless telegraphy within the territorial or
                    jurisdictional waters of Uruguay, except as provided in the dispositions adopted
                    by the national authorities; and which contains rules and regulations to be
                    observed by private corporations or persons who may desire to establish and
                    operate stations for wireless telegraphy in this Republic.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1108-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nicolay A. Grevstad</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
